        "id": "p1-b0",
        "type": "text",
        "text": "1. Concepts and examples",
        "tableHtml": null,
        "bbox": [
          0.10185185185185185,
          0.10540540540540541,
          0.4962962962962963,
          0.13378378378378378
        ],
        "headingLevel": 2,
        "order": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p1-b1",
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This page is original demonstration material. It is included so that reviewers can inspect a fixed page, select its text, and navigate its outline without using a personal book.",
        "tableHtml": null,
        "bbox": [
          0.1,
          0.1608108108108108,
          0.6962962962962963,
          0.23378378378378378
        ],
        "headingLevel": null,
        "order": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "p1-b2",
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Definition 1.1. A relation describes how one quantity is associated with another. In the following example, the rule takes a number x and returns its square.",
        "tableHtml": null,
        "bbox": [
          0.1,
          0.26216216216216215,
          0.7796296296296297,
          0.33513513513513515
        ],
        "headingLevel": null,
        "order": 2
      },
      {
        "id": "p1-b3",
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Example. For x = 0, 1, 2, the corresponding values are 0, 1, 4. The table and drawing below present the same small example in two forms.",
        "tableHtml": null,
        "bbox": [
          0.1,
          0.36486486486486486,
          0.75,
          0.4135135135135135
        ],
        "headingLevel": null,
        "order": 3
      },
      {
        "id": "p1-b4",
        "type": "equation",
        "text": "f (x) = x \\text {   squared }",
        "tableHtml": null,
        "bbox": [
          0.37777777777777777,
          0.5256756756756756,
          0.6148148148148148,
          0.5554054054054054
        ],
        "headingLevel": null,
        "order": 4
      },
      {
        "id": "p1-b5",
        "type": "table",
        "text": "x\tf(x)\n0\t0\n1\t1\n2\t4",
        "tableHtml": "<table><tr><td>x</td><td>f(x)</td></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>4</td></tr></table>",
        "bbox": [
